            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
              with
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalences"} weak equivalences
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphisms"} quasi-isomorphisms
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrations"} fibrations
                  the (degreewise)
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphisms"} epimorphisms
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrations"} cofibrations
                  the degreewise
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+monomorphism"} split injections
                  with cofibrant
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernel"} cokernel
            %p
          (For partial characterization of the
          %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+objects"} cofibrant objects
          see further
          = succeed ".)" do
            %a{:href => "#BoundedBelowComplexesOfProjectivesAreProjectivelyCofibrant"} below
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              Properness and cofibrant generation are discussed in
              %a{:href => "#HoveyPalmieriStrickland97"} Hovey, Palmieri &amp; Strickland (1997), remark after theorem 9.3.1
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#SchwedeShipley98"} Schwede &amp; Shipley (1998), p. 7
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#Fausk06"} Fauk (2006), Thm. 3.2
              %a{:href => "#Hovey99"} Hovey (1999), Lem. 2.3.6
              and that of the generating cofibrations are made explicit in
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#Hovey99"} Hovey (1999), Def. 2.3.3
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#MuroRoitzheim19"} Muro &amp; Roitzheim (2019), pp. 3
            %p#LocalPresentability
              It remains to see that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+chain+complexes"} category of chain complexes
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mod"} Mod
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+abelian+category"} Grothendieck abelian category
                  (by
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %a{:href => "Grothendieck+category#CateoriesOfModules"} this example
              %li
                %p
                  when
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒜
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
                  is a Grothendieck abelian category then so is
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Ch
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝒜
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ch_\bullet(\mathcal{A})
                  (by
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %a{:href => "Grothendieck+category#ChainComplexesInGrothAbCat"} this example
              %li
                %p
                  all Grothendick abelian categories are locally presentable (by
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a{:href => "locally+presentable+category#GrothAbCatsAreLocPresntbl"} this example
            %p
          %p
          #NotAllUnboundedComplexesAreProjectivelyCofibrant.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              It is clear that every chain complex in the model structure of Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StandardModelStructureOnUnboundedComplexes"}
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+object"} fibrant
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fields"} fields
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UnboundedChainComplexOfVectorSpacesProjectivelyCofibrant"}
              below)
              %em not
              every chain complex is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+object"} cofibrant
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+modules"} projective modules
              – a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/counterexample"} counterexample
              is given in
              = succeed ":" do
                %a{:href => "#Hovey99"} Hovey (1999), Rem. 2.3.7
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕂
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{K}
              any
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi 𝕂
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi 𝕂
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \coloneqq \mathbb{K} \oplus \mathbb{K} \cdot x
              be its
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+of+dual+numbers"} ring of dual numbers
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mn 2
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^2 = 0
            %p
              Denote its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/augmented+algebra"} augmentation
              by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mi ϵ
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi 𝕂
                            %mo ⊕
                            %mi 𝕂
                            %mo ⋅
                            %mi x
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi 𝕂
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi a
                            %mo +
                            %mi b
                            %mi x
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathllap{
                    \\epsilon
                    \\;\colon\;
                    }
                    \\mathbb{K} \oplus \mathbb{K} \cdot x
                    \&amp;\longrightarrow&amp;
                    \\mathbb{K}
                    \\\
                    a + b x &amp;\mapsto&amp; a
                    }
            %p
              Via this
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+homomorphism"} ring homomorphism
              we regard
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕂
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{K}
              as an
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            %p
              Now in the category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Ch
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi R
                      %mi Mod
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ch_\bullet(R Mod)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo →
                      %mi 𝕂
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mi 𝕂
                      %mi x
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mi x
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi 𝕂
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mi 𝕂
                      %mi x
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mi x
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi 𝕂
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mi 𝕂
                      %mi x
                      %mo →
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{A}
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\left(
                    \\cdots
                    \\to
                    \\mathbb{K} \oplus \mathbb{K}x
                    \\xrightarrow{
                    \\;\;
                    \\cdot x
                    \\;\;
                    }
                    \\mathbb{K} \oplus \mathbb{K}x
                    \\xrightarrow{
                    \\;\;
                    \\cdot x
                    \\;\;
                    }
                    \\mathbb{K} \oplus \mathbb{K}x
                    \\to
                    \\cdots
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Since its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+homology"} chain homology
              clearly vanishes in every degree, the morphism it receives out of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+object"} zero object
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphism
              and hence a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalence"} weak equivalence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %munder
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} W
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    0 \underset{\in \mathrm{W}}{\longrightarrow} \mathcal{A}
            %p
              and hence would be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/acyclic+cofibration"} acyclic cofibration
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
              were cofibrant.
            %p
              But consider then the following
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lifting+problem"} lifting problem
              with this morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                            %mi ⋯
                            %mo →
                            %mn 0
                            %mo →
                            %mn 0
                            %mo →
                            %mi R
                            %mo →
                            %mn 0
                            %mo →
                            %mn 0
                            %mo →
                            %mi ⋯
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "3em", :minsize => "3em"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "3em", :minsize => "3em"} ↓
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mi ϵ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi 𝒜
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mi ϵ
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                            %mi ⋯
                            %mo →
                            %mn 0
                            %mo →
                            %mn 0
                            %mo →
                            %mi 𝕂
                            %mo →
                            %mn 0
                            %mo →
                            %mn 0
                            %mo →
                            %mi ⋯
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                %mo ,
                                %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;\longrightarrow&amp;
                    \\big(
                    \\cdots \to 0 \to 0 \to R \to 0 \to 0 \to \cdots
                    \\big)
                    \\\
                    \\Bigg\downarrow
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\Bigg\downarrow
                    {}^{
                    \\epsilon
                    }
                    \\\
                    \\mathcal{A}
                    \&amp;
                    \\overset{
                    \\;\;
                    \\epsilon
                    \\;\;\;
                    }{
                    \\longrightarrow
                    }
                    \&amp;
                    \\big(
                    \\cdots \to 0 \to 0 \to \mathbb{K} \to 0 \to 0 \to \cdots
                    \\big)
                    \\mathrlap{\,,.}
                    }
            %p
              Since the morphism on the right is clearly degreewise surjective and hence a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration"} fibration
              in the model structure, cofibrancy of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
              would imply that a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lift"} lift
              in this diagram exists. But to be even a lift of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+modules"} graded modules
              this lift would have to be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphism"} identity morphism
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              in degree 0, in order to make (in degree 0), this
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
              of
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commute
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mo
                                  %mi id
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mo
                                  %mi ϵ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi ϵ
                          %mtd
                            %mi 𝕂
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; R
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \mathllap{^{id}}\nearrow
                    \&amp; \downarrow \mathrlap{^\epsilon}
                    \\\
                    R &amp;\underset{\epsilon}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \mathbb{K}
                    }
            %p
              But that underlying lift fails to be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+map"} chain map
              in degrees (-1,0), where the following
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
              does
              %em not
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commute
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi 𝕂
                            %mo ⊕
                            %mi 𝕂
                            %mi x
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mo
                                  %mi id
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} ↑
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathcolor => "red"}
                              %mo ×
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} ↑
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mo
                                  %mi id
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi 𝕂
                            %mo ⊕
                            %mi 𝕂
                            %mi x
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mo ⋅
                                %mi x
                          %mtd
                            %mi 𝕂
                            %mo ⊕
                            %mi 𝕂
                            %mi x
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    0
                    \&amp;\longrightarrow&amp;
                    \\mathbb{K} \oplus \mathbb{K}x
                    \\\
                    \\mathllap{^{id}}
                    \\Big\uparrow
                    \&amp;\color{red}\times&amp;
                    \\Big\uparrow
                    \\mathrlap{^{id}}
                    \\\
                    \\mathbb{K} \oplus \mathbb{K}x
                    \&amp;\underset{\cdot x}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    \\mathbb{K} \oplus \mathbb{K}x
                    \\mathrlap{\,.}
                    }
            %p
              It follows that the lift does not exist, hence that we have found an object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
              in the model structure from Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StandardModelStructureOnUnboundedComplexes"}
              which is not cofibrant.
          %p On the other hand:
          %p
          #BoundedBelowComplexesOfProjectivesAreProjectivelyCofibrant.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded-below+chain+complexes"} bounded-below chain complexes
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+modules"} projective modules
                are projectively
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+object"} cofibrant
              %br/
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded-below+chain+complex"} bounded-below chain complex
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+modules"} projective modules
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+object"} cofibrant
              in the model structure of Prop.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StandardModelStructureOnUnboundedComplexes"}
          (
          %a{:href => "#Hovey99"}> Hovey (1999), Lem. 2.3.6
          )
          %p This implies:
          %p
          #UnboundedChainComplexOfVectorSpacesProjectivelyCofibrant.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              a
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
                  in the projective model structure
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Ch
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi k
                        %mi Mod
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ch_\bullet(k Mod)
                  (Prop.
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StandardModelStructureOnUnboundedComplexes"}
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+objects"} cofibrant
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrations"} cofibrations
                  are exactly the
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphisms"} monomorphisms
            %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              By the assumption that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              is a field, every
              = succeed "-module" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+module"} projective
              (
              %a{:href => "projective+module#ModuleOverAFieldIsProjective"}> this Prop.
              ). Therefore Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BoundedBelowComplexesOfProjectivesAreProjectivelyCofibrant"}
              says, in this situation, that every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded-below+chain+complex"} bounded-below chain complex
              is cofibrant Moreover, since every injection of vector spaces splits (
              %a{:href => "Vect#ShortExactSequencesSplit"}> here
              ) the characterization of cofibrations in Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StandardModelStructureOnUnboundedComplexes"}
              says that every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injection"} injection
              into a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded-below+chain+complex"} bounded-below chain complex
              of vector spaces is a cofibration (since its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernel"} cokernel
              is clearly itself bounded-below and hence cofibrant by the previous statement) .
            %p
              Now every chain complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_\bullet
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              of its stages of lower
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connective+covers"} connective covers
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi cn
                      %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mo •
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi cn
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mo •
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi cn
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mo •
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    cn_0 V_\bullet
                    \\hookrightarrow
                    cn_{-1} V_\bullet
                    \\hookrightarrow
                    cn_{-2} V_\bullet
                    \\hookrightarrow
                    \\cdots
                    \\,.
            %p
              By the previous paragraph,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi cn
                      %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cn_0 V_\bullet
              is cofibrant and each morphism in this
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cotower"} cotower
              is a cofibration. Therefore
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi cn
                      %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mo •
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cn_0 V_\bullet \hookrightarrow V_\bullet
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transfinite+composition"} transfinite composition
              of cofibrations, hence a cofibration, and therefore
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_\bullet
              is cofibrant.
            %p
              This proves the first statement. From this the second follows by the characterization of the cofibrations in Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StandardModelStructureOnUnboundedComplexes"}
              and using again that all injections here are split.
          (Alternatively one may argue via the generating cofibration, cf.
          = succeed ".)" do
            %a{:href => "https://math.stackexchange.com/a/2457259/58526"} MO:a/2457259
          %p
          #MonoidalProjectiveModelStructureOnUnboundedChainComplexes.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+chain+complexes"} tensor product of chain complexes
              makes the projective model structure on unbounded chain complexes
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ch_\bullet(R Mod)
              (Prop.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StandardModelStructureOnUnboundedComplexes"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
          For the special case that all
          %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submodules"} submodules
          of
          %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+modules"} free modules
          are again free (such as over
          %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
            %semantics
              %mrow
                %mi R
                %mo =
                %mi ℤ
              %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R = \mathbb{Z}
          the
          = succeed "," do
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
          = succeed "," do
            %a{:href => "free+abelian+group#SubgroupsOfFreeAbelianGroupsAreFree"} this Prop.
          %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
            %semantics
              %mrow
                %mi R
                %mo =
                %mi k
              %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R = k
          a
          %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
          by
          = succeed "," do
            %a{:href => "free+module#EveryModuleOverAFieldIsFree"} this Prop
          %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
            %semantics
              %mrow
                %mi R
              %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          a
          = succeed "," do
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+ideal+domain"} principal ideal domain
          = succeed ")" do
            %a{:href => "free+module#submod"} this Prop.
          = succeed "." do
            %a{:href => "#Strickland20"} Strickland (2020), Prop. 25
          %a{:href => "#Hovey01"} Hovey (2001), Cor. 3.7
          %a{:href => "#Fausk06"} Fausk (2006), Thm. 6.1
          (who state an even more general result about
          %em
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaves"} sheaves
          of chain complexes).
          %p
          #LocalizedReedyModelStructureOnSimplicialUnboundedChainComplexes.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+simplicial+objects"} category of simplicial objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sCh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mi Mod
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sCh(R Mod)_\bullet
              in the projective model structure on unbounded chain complexes (from Prop.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BoundedBelowComplexesOfProjectivesAreProjectivelyCofibrant"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
              (obtained as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} left Bousfield localization
              of the
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reedy+model+structure"} Reedy model structure
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphisms"} quasi-isomorphisms
              under the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+chain+complex"} total chain complex
              functor, and such that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalent
              via :
            #eq:QuillenEquivalenceBetweenProjectiveUnboundedChainAndSimpEnhancement.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi const
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⇄
                    %msub
                      %mi sCh
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi ev
                      %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    const
                    \\,\colon\,
                    Ch_\bullet(R Mod)
                    \\rightleftarrows
                    sCh_\bullet(R Mod)
                    \\,\colon\,
                    ev_0
                    \\,.
            %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              The existence as a simplicial model category and Quillen equivalence of the underlying categories is due to
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#RezkSchwedeShipley01"} Rezk, Schwede &amp; Shipley (2001), cor. 4.6
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "simplicial+model+category#SimpEquivMods"} simplicial model category – Simplicial Quillen equivalent models
            %p Moreover, general facts imply that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a Reedy model structure with coefficients in a combinatorial model category is itself combinatorial (see
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "Reedy+model+structure#CombinatorialStructure"} here
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+Bousfield+localization"} left Bousfield localization
                  of a combinatorial model category is itself combinatorial (see
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a{:href => "Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories#Existence"} here
            %p
          %p
            Below, this model structure is recovered as example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CategoricalProjectiveClasses"}
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#InUnboundedDegreeGeneralResults"} Christensen-Hovey projective class construction
          %p
          #OverGroundFieldAllObjectsInSimplicialStructureOnUnboundedComplexesAreCofibrant.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              Over a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi sCh
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sCh_\bullet(k Mod)
              (from Prop.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalizedReedyModelStructureOnSimplicialUnboundedChainComplexes"}
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              Since
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} left Bousfield localization
              does not change the class of cofibrations, we need to show that every object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi V
                      %mo •
                      %mo •
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi sCh
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_\bullet^\bullet \in sCh_\bullet(k Mod)
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "Reedy+model+structure#ReedyModelStructure"} Reedy cofibrant
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "Reedy+model+structure#ReedyCofibrantObjects"} this Remark
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/latching+objects"} latching objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi r
                    %msubsup
                      %mi V
                      %mo •
                      %mi r
                    %mo →
                    %msubsup
                      %mi V
                      %mo •
                      %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_r V^r_\bullet \to V^r_\bullet
              are monomorphisms for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \in \mathbb{R}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ch_\bullet(k Mod)
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
              (cf.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a{:href => "category+of+chain+complexes#AbelianCategoryStructure"} here
              %a{:href => "Reedy+model+structure#LatchingInAbelianCategoryIsDegeneracySubobject"} this Prop.
              at
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reedy+model+structure"} Reedy model structure
              says that these are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphisms"} monomorphisms
              and hence the claim follows by Prop.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UnboundedChainComplexOfVectorSpacesProjectivelyCofibrant"}
          %p
          #MonoidalSimplicialEnhancementOfUnboundedChainModelStructure.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              At least over a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi sCh
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sCh_\bullet(k)
              from Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalizedReedyModelStructureOnSimplicialUnboundedChainComplexes"}
              becomes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
              via the
              = succeed "-object-wise" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Δ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+chain+complexes"} tensor product of chain complexes
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:QuillenEquivalenceBetweenProjectiveUnboundedChainAndSimpEnhancement"} (1)
              is a compatibly
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+Quillen+adjunction"} monoidal Quillen adjunction
              with respect to the corresponding monoidal model structure on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ch_\bullet(k)
              from Prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidalProjectiveModelStructureOnUnboundedChainComplexes"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidalProjectiveModelStructureOnUnboundedChainComplexes"}
          This ought to be compatible with the simplicial structure such as to give a
          = succeed "." do
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+monoidal+model+category"} simplicial monoidal model category
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              First, the plain
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reedy+model+structure"} Reedy model structure
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi sCh
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sCh_\bullet(k)
              becomes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
              under the objectwise
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+chain+complexes"} tensor product of chain complexes
              %a{:href => "monoidal+model+category#Barwick10"} Barwick (2010), Thm. 3.51
              (beware that the notation “
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{M}(A)
              ” there does refer to the Reedy model structure on
              = succeed "," do
                %em presheaves
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Func
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Func(A^{op}, \mathbf{M})
              (cf. p. 265), which means that the condition that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mo ←
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^{\leftarrow}
              consists of epimorphisms
              %em is
              satisfied for our case where, under this notational convention,
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo =
                      %mi Δ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = \Delta
            %p#SimplicialMonoidalModelStructure
              Next, to see that this monoidal model structure passes to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} left Bousfield localization
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi sCh
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sCh_\bullet(k)
              at the realization equivalences:
            %p
              Observing that every object in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sCh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sCh(k)
              is a simplicial homotopy colimit of simplicially constant objects (by an argument as in
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "homotopy+limit#SimplicialSetIsHomotopyColimitOverItself"} this Prop.
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sCh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sCh(k)
              are the homotopically constant simplicial objects, it is sufficient to check — by
              %a{:href => "Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories#Barwick10"} Barwick (2010), Prop. 4.47
              — that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi Ch
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \,\in\, Ch(k)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi.mathscript 𝒲
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi sCh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{W} \,\in\, sCh(k)
              homotopically constant, also their
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi const
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi.mathscript 𝒲
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi sCh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [const(V),\,\mathscr{W}] \,\in\, sCh(k)
              is homotopically constant.
            %p
              Now, on general grounds, the internal hom in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sCh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sCh(k)
              is given by an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/end"} end
              over the internal hom in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ch
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ch(k)
              (to be denoted by the same angular bracket notation), as follows:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi.mathscript 𝒱
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi.mathscript 𝒲
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ↦
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi s
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Δ
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} [
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi.mathscript 𝒱
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi.mathscript 𝒲
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo ′
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [\mathscr{V},\,\mathscr{W}]
                    \\;\colon\;
                    [s]
                    \\;\mapsto\;
                    \\int_{[s'] \in \Delta}
                    \\big[
                    (\Delta[s] \cdot \mathscr{V})_{s'}
                    ,\,
                    \\mathscr{W}_{s'}
                    \\big]
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)\cdot(-)
              denotes the canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensoring"} tensoring
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sCh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sCh(k)
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            %p
              So in the case at hand, where
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi.mathscript 𝒱
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi const
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{V} \,=\, const(V)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "left", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi const
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi V
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mi.mathscript 𝒲
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi s
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo ↦
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ∫
                            %mrow
                              %mi s
                              %mo ′
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} [
                          %mi Δ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi s
